"<div class=\"brand-bar\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"brand-logo\"><div class=\"brand-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div></div>\n<header class=\"lk-hd\"><div class=\"lk-topic\"><svg class=\"ic\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M4 20l1-4.2L16.2 4.6a1.6 1.6 0 0 1 2.3 0l.9.9a1.6 1.6 0 0 1 0 2.3L8.2 19z\"/><path d=\"M14.5 6.4l3.1 3.1\"/></svg></div><div class=\"lk-kicker\">Übung</div><div class=\"lk-big\">28</div><h1>zu 부정형</h1><div class=\"lk-de\">Der Infinitiv mit zu</div><div class=\"lk-intro\">Lektion 28의 문법을 직접 풀어 보며 익혀요.<br>B1 수준의 문장으로, 기본 16 · 중간 8 · 도전 6 문제를 풀어요.<div class=\"x-goals\"><div class=\"x-goals-t\">이 연습에서 확인할 것</div><div class=\"x-goal\">zu 부정형을 만들고, 분리동사는 aufzustehen처럼 한 단어로 써요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">zu 부정형과 함께 쓰는 말과, 화법조동사·lassen 뒤처럼 zu를 붙이지 않는 경우를 구별해요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">um … zu · ohne … zu · statt … zu와 damit · dass 문장 가운데 알맞은 것을 골라요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">lassen과 haben … zu · sein … zu · scheinen … zu의 뜻을 알아요</div></div><div class=\"x-goals\" style=\"margin-top:14px\"><div class=\"x-goals-t\">풀이 방법</div><div class=\"x-goal\">보기를 고르거나, 빈칸에 쓰거나, 단어를 눌러 문장을 만들어요</div><div class=\"x-goal\">빈칸 옆 괄호와 한국어 뜻이 힌트예요. 대문자와 소문자는 구별하지 않아요</div></div></div></header>\n<div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge review-badge\">기본</span><span class=\"sub-title\">기본 문제 · 배운 내용을 그대로 확인해요</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\">\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">1.</strong> aussteigen(내리다)의 zu 부정형은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) auszusteigen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) ausgezusteigen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) zu aussteigen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) aussteigenzu</button></div><div class=\"qe\">분리동사는 접두어와 동사 사이에 zu를 넣어 한 단어로 써요 — aus + zu + steigen.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">2.</strong> erzählen(이야기하다)의 zu 부정형은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) erzuzählen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) erzählenzu</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) zu erzählt</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) zu erzählen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">er-는 비분리 접두어라서 zu를 앞에 따로 써요 — zu erzählen.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;zu ziehen&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">3.</strong> Meine Eltern haben beschlossen, im Herbst ans Meer <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:11ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(ziehen)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">부모님은 가을에 바닷가로 이사하기로 결정했어요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Meine Eltern haben beschlossen, im Herbst ans Meer <b>zu ziehen</b>.</div>beschließen 뒤에는 zu 부정형이 와요. zu + 원형이 맨 끝이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;auszuschalten&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">4.</strong> Vergiss bitte nicht, den Herd <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:15ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(ausschalten)</span>!</div><div class=\"qko\">가스레인지 끄는 거 잊지 마!</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Vergiss bitte nicht, den Herd <b>auszuschalten</b>!</div>ausschalten은 분리동사라서 aus + zu + schalten을 붙여 써요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;zu finden&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">5.</strong> Es ist nicht leicht, in einer fremden Stadt Freunde <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:11ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(finden)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">낯선 도시에서 친구를 사귀기는 쉽지 않아요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Es ist nicht leicht, in einer fremden Stadt Freunde <b>zu finden</b>.</div>es ist + 형용사 뒤에는 zu 부정형이 와요. 목적어 Freunde는 그 앞에 놓여요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;arbeiten&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">6.</strong> Wir müssen heute länger im Büro <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:10ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(arbeiten)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">우리는 오늘 사무실에서 더 오래 일해야 해요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Wir müssen heute länger im Büro <b>arbeiten</b>.</div>화법조동사 뒤의 원형에는 zu를 붙이지 않아요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qr\" data-t=\"order\" data-a=\"[&quot;Jeden Abend höre ich die Nachbarn streiten.&quot;,&quot;Ich höre jeden Abend die Nachbarn streiten.&quot;,&quot;Ich höre die Nachbarn jeden Abend streiten.&quot;]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">7.</strong> 단어를 알맞은 순서로 놓으세요.</div><div class=\"qko\">저녁마다 이웃 사람들이 싸우는 소리가 들려요.</div><div class=\"qbuild\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div class=\"qpool\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"0\">Nachbarn</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"1\">die</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"2\">streiten.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"3\">Abend</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"4\">höre</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"5\">Jeden</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"6\">ich</button></div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"clr\">지우기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · <b>Jeden Abend höre ich die Nachbarn streiten.</b></div>hören 뒤의 원형에는 zu가 없어요. 원형 streiten은 맨 끝이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;lässt&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">8.</strong> Sie <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:7ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(lassen)</span> ihre Kinder am Wochenende lange schlafen.</div><div class=\"qko\">그녀는 주말에 아이들이 늦잠을 자게 둬요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Sie <b>lässt</b> ihre Kinder am Wochenende lange schlafen.</div>lassen은 sie(그녀)에서 a가 ä로 바뀌어요 — sie lässt. 원형 schlafen에는 zu가 없어요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;Lass&quot;,&quot;Lasst&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">9.</strong> <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:7ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(lassen)</span> uns heute Abend Pizza bestellen!</div><div class=\"qko\">오늘 저녁엔 피자 시키자!</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · <b>Lass</b> uns heute Abend Pizza bestellen!</div>제안은 Lass uns + 원형이에요. 여러 사람에게 말하면 Lasst uns도 돼요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">10.</strong> Er nimmt ein Taxi, <span class=\"qblank\"></span> den Flug nicht zu verpassen.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) ohne</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) damit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) um</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) statt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">택시를 타는 사람과 비행기를 놓치지 않으려는 사람이 같아요. 그래서 목적은 um … zu예요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">11.</strong> Er hat die Rechnung bezahlt, <span class=\"qblank\"></span> einen Blick darauf zu werfen. (쳐다보지도 않고)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) um</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) ohne</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) damit</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) statt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">'~하지 않고'는 ohne … zu예요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;Statt&quot;,&quot;Anstatt&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">12.</strong> <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:9ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(~하는 대신)</span> das Fahrrad selbst zu reparieren, hat er es in die Werkstatt gebracht.</div><div class=\"qko\">자전거를 직접 고치는 대신 그는 그것을 정비소에 맡겼어요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · <b>Statt</b> das Fahrrad selbst zu reparieren, hat er es in die Werkstatt gebracht.</div>'~하는 대신'은 (an)statt … zu예요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;zu schreiben&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">13.</strong> Ich kann heute nicht ausgehen, ich habe noch einen Bericht <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:14ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(schreiben)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">오늘은 외출할 수 없어요, 아직 보고서를 써야 하거든요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Ich kann heute nicht ausgehen, ich habe noch einen Bericht <b>zu schreiben</b>.</div>haben + zu 부정형은 '~해야 한다'라는 뜻이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">14.</strong> Der Drucker scheint kaputt <span class=\"qblank\"></span>.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) zu ist</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">b) zu sein</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) sein</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) ist zu</button></div><div class=\"qe\">scheinen + zu 부정형은 '~인 것 같다'예요 — scheint kaputt zu sein.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qr\" data-t=\"order\" data-a=\"[&quot;Ich habe keine Zeit, die ganze Wohnung aufzuräumen.&quot;]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">15.</strong> 단어를 알맞은 순서로 놓으세요.</div><div class=\"qko\">집 전체를 치울 시간이 없어요.</div><div class=\"qbuild\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div class=\"qpool\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"0\">habe</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"1\">die</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"2\">Zeit,</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"3\">aufzuräumen.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"4\">ganze</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"5\">Ich</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"6\">keine</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"7\">Wohnung</button></div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"clr\">지우기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · <b>Ich habe keine Zeit, die ganze Wohnung aufzuräumen.</b></div>Zeit haben 뒤에 zu 부정형이 와요. 목적어 die ganze Wohnung이 앞, aufzuräumen이 끝이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">16.</strong> Diese Handschrift ist kaum zu lesen. — 뜻은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) 이 글씨는 거의 읽지 않아요</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) 이 글씨를 읽으려고 해요</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) 이 글씨를 읽고 싶지 않아요</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) 이 글씨는 거의 읽을 수 없어요</button></div><div class=\"qe\">sein + zu 부정형은 '~될 수 있다'라는 뜻이에요. kaum(거의 ~않다)과 함께 '거의 읽을 수 없다'예요.</div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">중간</span><span class=\"sub-title\">중간 문제 · 조건이 한두 개 더 붙어요</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\">\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;abzuholen&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">17.</strong> Sie hat versprochen, uns am Bahnhof <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:11ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(abholen)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">그녀는 우리를 역에서 데리러 오겠다고 약속했어요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Sie hat versprochen, uns am Bahnhof <b>abzuholen</b>.</div>versprechen 뒤에 zu 부정형이 와요. abholen은 분리동사라서 abzuholen이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">18.</strong> Der Lehrer erwartet, <span class=\"qblank\"></span>. (우리가 숙제를 제때 내기를)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) dass wir die Hausaufgaben pünktlich abgeben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) die Hausaufgaben pünktlich abzugeben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) wir die Hausaufgaben pünktlich abzugeben</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) um die Hausaufgaben pünktlich abzugeben</button></div><div class=\"qe\">숙제를 내는 사람(wir)이 주문장에 없어요. 그래서 zu 부정형이 아니라 dass 문장이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">19.</strong> Ich rate dir, <span class=\"qblank\"></span>. (표를 일찍 사라고)</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) die Tickets früh zu kaufen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) die Tickets zu früh kaufen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) um die Tickets früh zu kaufen</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) dass du die Tickets früh zu kaufen</button></div><div class=\"qe\">표를 사는 사람은 주문장의 dir예요. 그래서 zu 부정형으로 써요 — 목적어가 앞, zu kaufen이 끝.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;lassen&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">20.</strong> Wir haben unsere Küche letztes Jahr komplett erneuern <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:8ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(lassen)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">우리는 작년에 부엌을 완전히 새로 고쳤어요(업체에 맡겨서).</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Wir haben unsere Küche letztes Jahr komplett erneuern <b>lassen</b>.</div>원형과 함께 쓴 lassen은 현재완료에서도 lassen 그대로예요 — erneuern lassen.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;gelassen&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">21.</strong> Hast du den Schlüssel schon wieder im Auto <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:10ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(lassen)</span>?</div><div class=\"qko\">열쇠를 또 차에 두고 온 거야?</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Hast du den Schlüssel schon wieder im Auto <b>gelassen</b>?</div>원형 없이 '두다'로 쓰면 과거분사는 gelassen이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qr\" data-t=\"order\" data-a=\"[&quot;Er steht jeden Tag um fünf auf, um vor der Arbeit zu joggen.&quot;,&quot;Jeden Tag steht er um fünf auf, um vor der Arbeit zu joggen.&quot;]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">22.</strong> 단어를 알맞은 순서로 놓으세요.</div><div class=\"qko\">그는 출근 전에 조깅하려고 매일 다섯 시에 일어나요.</div><div class=\"qbuild\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div class=\"qpool\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"0\">der</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"1\">auf,</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"2\">Tag</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"3\">steht</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"4\">zu</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"5\">fünf</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"6\">jeden</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"7\">um</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"8\">joggen.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"9\">Arbeit</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"10\">um</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"11\">Er</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"12\">vor</button></div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"clr\">지우기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · <b>Er steht jeden Tag um fünf auf, um vor der Arbeit zu joggen.</b></div>주문장은 분리동사 auf가 끝, 쉼표 뒤에 um … zu joggen이 와요.<br>um fünf(시각)와 um … zu(목적)를 구별해요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">23.</strong> Die Kinder sind aus dem Haus gegangen, <span class=\"qblank\"></span> ihre Mutter es bemerkt hat.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">a) ohne dass</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) ohne zu</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) um</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) statt</button></div><div class=\"qe\">주어가 다르고(Kinder · Mutter) 뒤에 문장이 와요. 그래서 ohne dass예요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;gehen&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">24.</strong> Mein Chef lässt mich manchmal früher nach Hause <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:7ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(gehen)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">사장님은 가끔 나를 일찍 집에 보내 줘요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Mein Chef lässt mich manchmal früher nach Hause <b>gehen</b>.</div>lassen 뒤의 원형에는 zu가 없어요.</div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"sub-head\"><span class=\"sub-badge\">도전</span><span class=\"sub-title\">도전 문제 · 함정과 예외까지 따져 봐요</span></div><div class=\"quiz-block\">\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">25.</strong> 틀린 문장은?</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Du brauchst am Samstag nicht ins Büro zu kommen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich habe vor, nächstes Jahr ein Auslandssemester zu machen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">c) Ich habe gestern meinen Laptop reparieren lassen.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">d) Sie hat ihren Sohn das Zimmer aufzuräumen lassen.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">lassen 뒤의 원형에는 zu가 없어요 — das Zimmer aufräumen lassen.<br>nicht brauchen은 zu와 함께 써서 맞아요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;zu&quot;],[&quot;können&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">26.</strong> Sie hofft, dass sie nächstes Jahr in Wien studieren kann.<br>= Sie hofft, nächstes Jahr in Wien studieren <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:5ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"> <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:8ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 2\"><span class=\"qh\">(können)</span>.</div><div class=\"qko\">그녀는 내년에 빈에서 공부할 수 있기를 바라요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Sie hofft, dass sie nächstes Jahr in Wien studieren kann.<br>= Sie hofft, nächstes Jahr in Wien studieren <b>zu</b> <b>können</b>.</div>주어가 같아서 zu 부정형으로 줄여요. 화법조동사가 있으면 그 앞에 zu가 와요 — studieren zu können.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;zu treiben&quot;],[&quot;schwimmen&quot;],[&quot;zu sitzen&quot;],[&quot;lasse&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">27.</strong> Ich habe beschlossen, mehr Sport <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:12ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(treiben)</span>. Deshalb gehe ich jetzt dreimal in der Woche <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:11ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 2\"><span class=\"qh\">(schwimmen)</span>, statt abends vor dem Fernseher <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:11ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 3\"><span class=\"qh\">(sitzen)</span>. Morgen <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:7ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 4\"><span class=\"qh\">(lassen)</span> ich mir von einem Trainer einen Plan erstellen.</div><div class=\"qko\">운동을 더 하기로 결심했어요. 그래서 이제 저녁에 TV 앞에 앉아 있는 대신 일주일에 세 번 수영하러 가요. 내일은 트레이너에게 계획을 짜 달라고 할 거예요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Ich habe beschlossen, mehr Sport <b>zu treiben</b>. Deshalb gehe ich jetzt dreimal in der Woche <b>schwimmen</b>, statt abends vor dem Fernseher <b>zu sitzen</b>. Morgen <b>lasse</b> ich mir von einem Trainer einen Plan erstellen.</div>beschließen·statt 뒤는 zu 부정형이에요.<br>gehen(이동의 목적)과 lassen 뒤의 원형에는 zu가 없어요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">28.</strong> 두 문장을 바르게 이은 것은?<br>Ich spare jeden Monat Geld. Meine Tochter soll später studieren können.</div><div class=\"qg\"><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">a) Ich spare jeden Monat Geld, um meine Tochter später studieren zu können.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">b) Ich spare jeden Monat Geld, um später meine Tochter studieren kann.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"1\">c) Ich spare jeden Monat Geld, damit meine Tochter später studieren kann.</button><button class=\"qo\" data-c=\"0\">d) Ich spare jeden Monat Geld, damit meine Tochter später zu studieren kann.</button></div><div class=\"qe\">돈을 모으는 사람(ich)과 공부할 사람(Tochter)이 달라요. 그래서 um … zu가 아니라 damit이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qr\" data-t=\"order\" data-a=\"[&quot;Statt sich zu beeilen, trinkt er in aller Ruhe noch einen Kaffee.&quot;,&quot;Statt sich zu beeilen, trinkt er noch in aller Ruhe einen Kaffee.&quot;]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">29.</strong> 단어를 알맞은 순서로 놓으세요.</div><div class=\"qko\">그는 서두르는 대신 느긋하게 커피를 한 잔 더 마셔요.</div><div class=\"qbuild\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div><div class=\"qpool\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"0\">trinkt</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"1\">er</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"2\">Kaffee.</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"3\">Ruhe</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"4\">noch</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"5\">Statt</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"6\">einen</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"7\">zu</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"8\">beeilen,</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"9\">in</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"10\">sich</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qc\" data-i=\"11\">aller</button></div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"clr\">지우기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · <b>Statt sich zu beeilen, trinkt er in aller Ruhe noch einen Kaffee.</b></div>statt … zu 부분이 첫 자리라서 주문장은 동사 trinkt로 시작해요.<br>재귀동사는 sich zu beeilen이에요.</div></div>\n<div class=\"qi qf\" data-t=\"fill\" data-a=\"[[&quot;zu verstehen&quot;],[&quot;zu wissen&quot;]]\"><div class=\"qq\"><strong class=\"qn\">30.</strong> Die Gebrauchsanweisung ist kaum <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:14ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 1\"><span class=\"qh\">(verstehen)</span>, und der Verkäufer scheint selbst nicht genau <input class=\"qin\" type=\"text\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocapitalize=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" style=\"width:11ch\" aria-label=\"빈칸 2\"><span class=\"qh\">(wissen)</span>, wie das Gerät funktioniert.</div><div class=\"qko\">사용 설명서는 거의 이해할 수가 없고, 판매원도 기기가 어떻게 작동하는지 정확히 모르는 것 같아요.</div><div class=\"qa\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb\" data-q=\"chk\">확인</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"show\">정답 보기</button><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"redo\">다시 풀기</button></div><div class=\"qe\"><div class=\"qsol\">정답 · Die Gebrauchsanweisung ist kaum <b>zu verstehen</b>, und der Verkäufer scheint selbst nicht genau <b>zu wissen</b>, wie das Gerät funktioniert.</div>sein + zu 부정형은 '~될 수 있다', scheinen + zu 부정형은 '~인 것 같다'예요.</div></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"qscore\" data-total=\"30\" data-no-print><div class=\"qscore-t\">맞힌 문제 <b class=\"qscore-n\">0</b> / 30</div><div class=\"qscore-bar\"><i></i></div><button type=\"button\" class=\"qb is-ghost\" data-q=\"all\">모두 다시 풀기</button></div>\n<div class=\"brand-foot\"><img src=\"%%A0%%\" alt=\"Sophia Deutsch Akademie\" class=\"foot-logo\"><div class=\"foot-name\">Sophia Deutsch Akademie</div><div class=\"foot-tag\">Innovative Learning Beyond the Traditional</div></div>"